---
description: Do not use Unity script execution order to sequence gameplay
alwaysApply: true
---

# No execution order

Do not use `[DefaultExecutionOrder]`, and do not set `executionOrder` in a script `.meta`. Leave it at `0`.

If one object must run after another, call it from the first (`ShipBase` moves, then tells riders to follow). Do not rely on Unity sorting `Update` / `LateUpdate` / `FixedUpdate`.

```csharp
// BAD
[DefaultExecutionOrder(200)]
public sealed class ShipBase : MonoBehaviour {
    private void LateUpdate() {
        transform.position = EvaluateFlightPosition();
    }
}

// GOOD — explicit call, default order
public sealed class ShipBase : MonoBehaviour {
    private void LateUpdate() {
        transform.position = EvaluateFlightPosition();
        FollowRiders();
    }
}
```
